Four of the frontend tests could not fail before the implementation existed --
absence assertions pass trivially while the thing they watch is unbuilt -- and
there is no coverage tooling on that side at all, so this pass is the only
instrument that can say they hold anything up. `the badge is derived from the
payload` and `the rail drops its footer` both turn them red; the second takes
20 tests with it.
